    <string name="compass_go">USE THE COMPASS</string>
    <string name="compass_stop">KEEP THIS</string>
    <string name="compass_hint">Back of the phone flat on the glass, screen to the room. Keep it away from radiators and metal frames.</string>
    <string name="window_view">Outside</string>
    <string name="window_delete">REMOVE THE WINDOW</string>
    <string name="vacation_intro">Going away? Here\'s who will want water and roughly when, by the forecast and each pot\'s own pace. Send it to whoever comes to water.</string>
    <string name="vacation_days">Days away</string>
    <string name="vacation_fine">will manage without water</string>
    <string name="vacation_share">SEND THE NOTE</string>
    <string name="vacation_note_head">Plants for the next %1$d days — thank you! 🌿</string>
    <string name="vacation_line">• %1$s (%2$s, %3$s): water around %4$s</string>
    <string name="vacation_none">• %1$s (%2$s, %3$s): no water needed</string>
    <string name="vacation_note_foot">Before watering, a finger in the soil: if it\'s still damp, wait. Water until it drains, then empty the saucer.</string>
    <string name="ob_1">Every plant at your window has a spirit. Catch them all: a photo, the species, the window it stands at.</string>
    <string name="ob_1b">Spirits live by the real thing: the real sun and clouds on their sill, real new leaves, real pests. They bask, pine, sleep through winter and change form as the plant grows.</string>
    <string name="ob_2">Where do you live? The light on each window comes from the real sky over your town.</string>
    <string name="ob_2b">Optional. Without a town the windows get the season\'s usual weather.</string>
    <string name="ob_3">Now the first window: the one your plants stand at.</string>
    <string name="ob_3b">You can add more windows later.</string>
    <string name="ob_4">No watering calendar here.</string>
    <string name="ob_4b">I estimate how fast each pot dries from its sun and the heating, and ask you to touch the soil when it\'s time. Your finger teaches me your home.</string>
